; A type answered through a bare `Int` result is refused as AX3004,
; parameterised or not (MM-VAL-24).
;
; `leak` is the parameterised case. `(Result Int Error)` through an
; `Int` keeps the address and throws the type arguments away, so
; nothing downstream can recover what it holds. Measured twice on
; 2026-08-26, both silent at the time: `IO.makeDir` declared `Int` over
; a body that had become `sysMkdir`'s `Result` and returned a heap
; address where an errno belonged, and `driver.runTool` did the same
; one layer up and surfaced as `AX4003` at run time.
;
; `mkSpan` is the monomorphic case, a struct through `Int`, refused the
; same way. `1240-record-through-int.ax` pins it beside its fixes.
(import Err)

(struct Span
  (a : Int)
  (b : Int))

; A monomorphic struct through `Int`.
(:: mkSpan (-> Int Int Int))
(fn (mkSpan a b)
  (Span a b))

; The defect: a parameterised type through `Int`.
(:: leak (-> Int Int))
(fn (leak x)
  (Ok x))

(:: main Int)
(fn (main)
  (mkSpan 1 2))
